{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":14898,"num_turns":6,"result":"Fixed `lru.py`. The cache now uses an `OrderedDict` with explicit recency tracking:\n\n- `get` moves the accessed key to the most-recent end and returns `default` (`None`) on a miss without touching order.\n- `put` on an existing key updates the value, bumps recency, and evicts nothing; on a new key it inserts and evicts the least-recently-used entry only when over capacity.\n- `__len__` and `__contains__` are implemented, and `in` only reads membership, so it never changes recency.\n- `LRUCache(capacity < 1)` raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe existing test in `tests/` passes, and I verified each issue point with a direct script (eviction after `get`, update-without-eviction, defaults, `len`/`in`, and the `ValueError`).","session_id":"44dab606-7adf-416c-bad7-a716e757f7df","usage":{"input_tokens":2221,"output_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":56320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"factory_credits":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"ttft_ms":1389.3333333333333}}
